      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Service Connections\nA service connection holds the credentials for\none outside system. For AWS, it holds an\naccess key or an OIDC setup, and optionally a\nrole to assume ([AWS connection doc](https://g\nithub.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-azurede\nvops/blob/v1.16.0/website/docs/r/serviceendpoi\nnt_aws.html.markdown)). A pipeline refers to a\nconnection by its name. Authorizations and\nchecks refer to it by its ID. The secrets can\nbe written but never read back, so Terraform\ncannot see a secret that someone changed in\nthe web interface.\n\nOIDC stands for OpenID Connect. With OIDC,\nAzure DevOps gives each run a short-lived\ntoken, and the outside system trusts that\ntoken instead of a stored key. Microsoft\nrecommends this workload identity federation\nover stored secrets ([security overview](https\n://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipe\nlines/security/overview)). The [authentication\nmap](../../authentication/authentication.md#wo\nrkload-identity-federation-workload-identity-f\nederation) explains the idea.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-59276aa14377",
      "originalText": "Service Connections\nA service connection holds the credentials for one outside system. For AWS, it holds an access key or an OIDC setup, and optionally a role to assume ([AWS connection doc](https://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-azuredevops/blob/v1.16.0/website/docs/r/serviceendpoint_aws.html.markdown)). A pipeline refers to a connection by its name. Authorizations and checks refer to it by its ID. The secrets can be written but never read back, so Terraform cannot see a secret that someone changed in the web interface.\n\nOIDC stands for OpenID Connect. With OIDC, Azure DevOps gives each run a short-lived token, and the outside system trusts that token instead of a stored key. Microsoft recommends this workload identity federation over stored secrets ([security overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/security/overview)). The [authentication map](../../authentication/authentication.md#workload-identity-federation-workload-identity-federation) explains the idea.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "service-connections"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
