    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9234333544,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-23758bfb109d",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1288.8,
      "y": 640.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 367.5,
      "seed": 763828,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Checks Live Outside the YAML\nMicrosoft puts it this way: \"Users modifying\nthe pipeline yaml file can't modify the\nchecks\" ([approvals and checks](https://learn.\nmicrosoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/pro\ncess/approvals)). Administrators of the\nresource manage its checks in the web\ninterface or in Terraform. So a check on an\nenvironment or a service connection protects\nproduction even when someone edits the\npipeline in a pull request.\n\nGates written in YAML are weaker. A\n`condition` on a stage, such as \"only on the\nmain branch\", lives in the same file that a\npull request can change. The task\n`ManualValidation` pauses a run in YAML, and\nany user with the Queue builds permission can\nresume it ([manual validation](https://learn.m\nicrosoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/task\ns/reference/manual-validation-v0)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-23758bfb109d",
      "originalText": "Checks Live Outside the YAML\nMicrosoft puts it this way: \"Users modifying the pipeline yaml file can't modify the checks\" ([approvals and checks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/process/approvals)). Administrators of the resource manage its checks in the web interface or in Terraform. So a check on an environment or a service connection protects production even when someone edits the pipeline in a pull request.\n\nGates written in YAML are weaker. A `condition` on a stage, such as \"only on the main branch\", lives in the same file that a pull request can change. The task `ManualValidation` pauses a run in YAML, and any user with the Queue builds permission can resume it ([manual validation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/tasks/reference/manual-validation-v0)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "checks-live-outside-the-yaml"
      }
    },
    {
