    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6310302718,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-a8444fec7d9e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1332.0,
      "y": 2196.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 665.0,
      "seed": 688594,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reading an Azure DevOps Configuration\n| Resource | Azure DevOps object | What to\ncheck |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `azuredevops_project` | project | Usually\nlooked up with a data source, not created |\n| `azuredevops_serviceendpoint_aws` | AWS\nservice connection | Static keys or\n`use_oidc`, role to assume |\n| `azuredevops_pipeline_authorization` |\npermission of a pipeline to use a resource |\n`pipeline_id` set, or open to all pipelines |\n| `azuredevops_serviceendpoint_permissions` |\nuser roles on a connection | Which groups may\nuse or administer it |\n| `azuredevops_variable_group` | variable\ngroup | Secret values in the state |\n| `azuredevops_environment`,\n`azuredevops_check_approval` | environment and\nits checks | Who approves, and for which\nstages |\n| `azuredevops_build_definition` | pipeline\ndefinition | YAML path, and triggers from YAML\nor the definition |\n\nRead the version constraint and the lock file\nfirst, because older versions behave\ndifferently. Then find the provider's\ncredential: a personal access token (PAT), a\nservice principal or a managed identity\n([provider docs](https://github.com/microsoft/\nterraform-provider-azuredevops/blob/v1.16.0/we\nbsite/docs/index.html.markdown)). Last,\ncompare each connection, variable group and\nenvironment with the\n`azuredevops_pipeline_authorization`\nresources. A resource without one was\nauthorized by hand.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-a8444fec7d9e",
      "originalText": "Reading an Azure DevOps Configuration\n| Resource | Azure DevOps object | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `azuredevops_project` | project | Usually looked up with a data source, not created |\n| `azuredevops_serviceendpoint_aws` | AWS service connection | Static keys or `use_oidc`, role to assume |\n| `azuredevops_pipeline_authorization` | permission of a pipeline to use a resource | `pipeline_id` set, or open to all pipelines |\n| `azuredevops_serviceendpoint_permissions` | user roles on a connection | Which groups may use or administer it |\n| `azuredevops_variable_group` | variable group | Secret values in the state |\n| `azuredevops_environment`, `azuredevops_check_approval` | environment and its checks | Who approves, and for which stages |\n| `azuredevops_build_definition` | pipeline definition | YAML path, and triggers from YAML or the definition |\n\nRead the version constraint and the lock file first, because older versions behave differently. Then find the provider's credential: a personal access token (PAT), a service principal or a managed identity ([provider docs](https://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-azuredevops/blob/v1.16.0/website/docs/index.html.markdown)). Last, compare each connection, variable group and environment with the `azuredevops_pipeline_authorization` resources. A resource without one was authorized by hand.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "reading-an-azdo-configuration"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3968064842,
      "isDeleted": false,
