    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8253481565,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-d53f60d12a3b",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1890.4,
      "y": 2456.5,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 280.0,
      "seed": 676190,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Apply Runs an Unreviewed Plan\nWhen the apply step runs without the saved\nplan file, Terraform makes a new plan and\napplies it at once, because the task adds\n`-auto-approve`. That new plan can differ from\nthe one that reviewers saw: drift, a merge in\nbetween, or a changed secret all count.\nHashiCorp says a plan made without `-out`\ngives no guarantee about what the apply will\ndo ([plan command](https://developer.hashicorp\n.com/terraform/cli/commands/plan)). Publish\nthe plan file and apply exactly that file. A\nsaved plan already holds the variable values,\nso the apply step must not pass `-var` again\n([apply command](https://developer.hashicorp.c\nom/terraform/cli/commands/apply)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d53f60d12a3b",
      "originalText": "Apply Runs an Unreviewed Plan\nWhen the apply step runs without the saved plan file, Terraform makes a new plan and applies it at once, because the task adds `-auto-approve`. That new plan can differ from the one that reviewers saw: drift, a merge in between, or a changed secret all count. HashiCorp says a plan made without `-out` gives no guarantee about what the apply will do ([plan command](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/commands/plan)). Publish the plan file and apply exactly that file. A saved plan already holds the variable values, so the apply step must not pass `-var` again ([apply command](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/commands/apply)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "apply-runs-unreviewed-plan"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1891109478,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-d4f38375ca88",
