      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Connection Role Ignored\nAn AWS service connection can name a role to\nassume. TerraformCLI exports only the keys and\nthe region, so Terraform runs as the IAM user\nbehind the keys, not as the role.\nConfigurations work around this with\n`assume_role` in the provider block. A run\nthat relies on the connection's role instead\nfails with \"AccessDenied\" or reaches the wrong\naccount.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d4f38375ca88",
      "originalText": "Connection Role Ignored\nAn AWS service connection can name a role to assume. TerraformCLI exports only the keys and the region, so Terraform runs as the IAM user behind the keys, not as the role. Configurations work around this with `assume_role` in the provider block. A run that relies on the connection's role instead fails with \"AccessDenied\" or reaches the wrong account.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "connection-role-ignored"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2719883518,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-2d13706f1a97",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
