    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9432358664,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-369753c7496c",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1890.4,
      "y": 3487.5,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 157.5,
      "seed": 384733,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Misspelled Environments\nWhen a pipeline names an environment that does\nnot exist, Azure Pipelines creates it\nautomatically when it can ([environments](http\ns://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pip\nelines/process/environments)). The new\nenvironment has no checks. So a typo in the\nenvironment name of a production stage removes\nits approval without any error.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-369753c7496c",
      "originalText": "Misspelled Environments\nWhen a pipeline names an environment that does not exist, Azure Pipelines creates it automatically when it can ([environments](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/process/environments)). The new environment has no checks. So a typo in the environment name of a production stage removes its approval without any error.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "misspelled-environments"
      }
    },
