      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1890.4,
      "y": 3962.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 210.0,
      "seed": 354927,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Secrets in State\nThe secret key of an AWS connection and the\nsecret values of a variable group sit in the\nstate in plain text. Anyone who can read the\nstate bucket can read them. Because the\nprovider never reads these secrets back, a\nsecret changed in the web interface never\nshows in a plan. A connection with `use_oidc`\nholds no secret at all ([AWS connection doc](h\nttps://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider\n-azuredevops/blob/v1.16.0/website/docs/r/servi\nceendpoint_aws.html.markdown#L55)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-ec13f18134d3",
      "originalText": "Secrets in State\nThe secret key of an AWS connection and the secret values of a variable group sit in the state in plain text. Anyone who can read the state bucket can read them. Because the provider never reads these secrets back, a secret changed in the web interface never shows in a plan. A connection with `use_oidc` holds no secret at all ([AWS connection doc](https://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-azuredevops/blob/v1.16.0/website/docs/r/serviceendpoint_aws.html.markdown#L55)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "azdo-secrets-in-state"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
