      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Renamed and Idle Connections\nA pipeline refers to a service connection by\nname, and an AWS role that trusts Azure DevOps\nthrough OIDC can also name it. Renaming the\nconnection in Terraform therefore breaks every\nYAML file and trust policy that uses the old\nname. Separately, Azure Pipelines can disable\na connection after 100 days without use\n([service connections](https://learn.microsoft\n.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/library/serv\nice-endpoints)). The provider has no field for\nthis state, so the plan stays clean while runs\nfail.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-c67b214a6d33",
      "originalText": "Renamed and Idle Connections\nA pipeline refers to a service connection by name, and an AWS role that trusts Azure DevOps through OIDC can also name it. Renaming the connection in Terraform therefore breaks every YAML file and trust policy that uses the old name. Separately, Azure Pipelines can disable a connection after 100 days without use ([service connections](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/library/service-endpoints)). The provider has no field for this state, so the plan stays clean while runs fail.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "renamed-and-idle-connections"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
